ET
q 0.7 0.75 0.8 rg 45 428 522 0.75 re f Q
BT
/F2 9.5 Tf
0.15 0.2 0.3 rg
50 414 Td
(A. Modifiable Behavioral Risk Factors:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
0.1 0.1 0.15 rg
55 401 Td
(  * Excessive dietary sodium consumption \(>2,300 mg/day\) and deficient potassium intake \(<3,500 mg/day\).) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
0.1 0.1 0.15 rg
55 388 Td
(  * Physical inactivity, sedentary lifestyle, and high prevalence of abdominal obesity \(BMI >=30\).) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
0.1 0.1 0.15 rg
55 375 Td
(  * Consumption of tobacco products \(cigarettes, shisha/hookah\) and harmful alcohol intake.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
0.1 0.1 0.15 rg
55 362 Td
(  * Diets high in saturated fats, trans-fatty acids, and refined sugars.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 9.5 Tf
0.15 0.2 0.3 rg
50 349 Td
(B. Non-Modifiable Risk Factors:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
0.1 0.1 0.15 rg
55 336 Td
(  * Advanced age \(>=65 years\) leading to physiological vascular elastance reduction and large artery stiffness) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
0.1 0.1 0.15 rg
55 323 Td
(  * Genetic predisposition and positive family history of early cardiovascular disease.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
0.1 0.1 0.15 rg
55 310 Td
(  * Co-existing chronic conditions: Diabetes mellitus, chronic kidney disease \(CKD\), and metabolic syndrome.) Tj
ET
